From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.storage.applicationdata: ApplicationDataCompositeValue

LanguageTool for Desktop (an app package) keeps settings grouped in an
ApplicationDataCompositeValue. The class did not exist: RoGetActivationFactory
failed, the app's start ended in a .NET exception, and it ran on with neither
a window nor a tray icon. The class is now activatable: an in-memory property
set (the PropertySet code with a second store beside the registry) whose class
name is Windows.Storage.ApplicationDataCompositeValue. Stored in a settings
container it is serialized as one value and read back as a composite; a
composite inside a composite is not stored.
---
